check point MUST
nodejs installed ->  https://nodejs.org/en/download #below you will see windows installer .msi
mongoDB Compass installed -> https://www.mongodb.com/products/tools/compass

in command prompt check
1. node -v 
2. mongosh 
3. mongod --version

#frontend code run command
1. go to frontend folder then run this command `npm start`

2. go to backend folder then run this command `npm start && node seeder.js`

if you want to edit the product to to this folder `mini-ecommerce\backend\data\products.json`
the change as per your needs.

again 
3. run this command `node seeder.js`


4. to terminate the running process  keyboard shortcut `ctrl + c`